% formalizes: def:renewal
% definition: Renewal
% says: Replacing a loan's due date with a new one, three weeks on.
% fidelity: strained — a renewal replaces the due date; Datalog adds facts and cannot replace one, so the new date is recorded beside the old, and "three weeks on" is a given relation, not arithmetic.
% renewal(R, L): R is a renewal of the loan L; renewal_on(R, D): made on day D.
renewed(L) :- renewal(_, L).
due_after_renewal(L, D2) :- renewal(R, L), renewal_on(R, D1), three_weeks_after(D1, D2).
